00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.629 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  marvel's avengers is a game which tries  to appeal to many types of gamers a  cinematic story with tons of set pieces  to a loot-based rpg with way more depth  than most people would expect  put bluntly marvel's avengers wants your  time for many years to come  and although nothing here is  revolutionary there is something very  special  in the making this is my 30-hour review  of marvel's avengers  to help you decide if this is the game  for you and spoiler alert  i like it  [Music]  marvel's avengers is split into two  elements the campaign and the online  co-operative rpg mode known as the  avengers initiative  both offer vastly different experiences  from the opening moments of the campaign  it's easy to see that this is a marvel  game made by fans  as everywhere we look we see easter eggs  and constant fan  service the main character of kamala  khan is a brilliant choice  to lead the reassembling of the avengers  after the events of ade  her positivity and constant fangirling  would usually be  an annoyance but kamala is written and  acted to perfection she's lovable and  her personality becomes infectious which  again comes down to the stellar writing  and voice acting on show here the  narrative  is another strong element as those  returning avengers  finally reunite to take down modok and  aim  and the cutscenes depict his slow  descent into madness taking many hours  to come to fruition  the story beats feel directly out of a  marvel comic book with each avenger  having their time to shine  in a campaign running around 8 to 10  hours in length  the avengers we play as all feel  drastically different and will  undoubtedly add replayability to both  the campaign  and the online avengers initiative for  example we don't get much of it but the  free running of captain america was  unlike any other character  and thor's fighting style well let's  just say if you liked playing as the god  of war on ps4 you'll feel right at home  with his abilities  throwing the ulna and summoning it back  to your hand never got old  and i played as thor for 20 hours  straight  similarly the super abilities of each  character felt distinctive  such as kamala's high five or black  widow's invisibility cloak  but here lies an issue how can hulk  smashing an enemy into oblivion  and a black widow punching a foe have  the same output  this really becomes an issue which  breaks the immersion  why does thor need to hit a henchman 12  times to take them down  this is the element of the game which  has been adapted to make all the  avengers as  balanced as possible even when it  doesn't seem like it should be  but if it didn't we'd all simply pick  hulk  marvel's avengers does attempt to keep  other areas of the law safe  using thor as an example his hammer  cannot be lifted by anyone  unworthy so when a hammer is on the  chest of an enemy  they are stuck there until thor sees fit  as we continue playing loot is thrown at  us each element of our character is  upgradable from  bracelets to bone density and everything  in between  but here's why that fails as a concept  nothing changes on the character at all  each new piece of gear we find  has zero impact on the aesthetics  for example we find the new chest piece  and apply it  and nothing happens it's all background  numbers and nothing is reflected in a  way which makes us want to chase the  loot  in other loot based video games each  item is reflected on your character  unlocking a full set of armor was a real  reward but here  this concept is tossed to the side for  something you may find sinister  or just another part of video games in  2020 a real money marketplace  in which outfits are bought and applied  to your characters  there are free versions too but at the  core the reason we don't see  iron man slowly evolve in game is to  incentivize us to buy a costume instead  and coincidentally there is a mission in  the game which perfectly sums up why  seeing our character armor update  is great by the time the credits roll  we've learned the basics of online play  using the war table to navigate and  continue  new elements of the story but right away  the story beats  evaporate there are cut scenes and  conjecture but the quality we saw in the  campaign  is nowhere to be seen now don't get me  wrong there are some inventive missions  but nothing comes close to that of the  campaign  and similarly the fighting mechanics we  learned over the story  are removed too take the taskmaster  fight at the start of the campaign  we learned to time a dodge and return  fire at the right moment  we learned how to attack with tactical  awareness and  now look at the task master boss fight  in the multiplayer portion  the difference is unnerving the fighting  online alongside other people  is boiled down to mindless bottom  bashing the abomination fight  is exactly the same there is a huge  weakness with online boss fights as  right now  the week of release there are no  mechanics in sight  if we take the game which is the closest  comparison destiny  who had a similar launch to this the  boss fights in there require precision  to find weak spots  they require knowledge of timing and  occasionally it was about being in the  perfect place  and understanding the boss's movements  but here in marvel's avengers  it's 10 minutes of spamming the buttons  and hoping you don't die  so you may think at this point that i  dislike this game when in fact  i think i'm addicted and it all comes  down to the loot system  we've looked at why it doesn't work in a  visual sense but underneath that  the depth of the loot system is  mind-blowing during the first 25 to  about 40 hours of your adventure you'll  simply be pressing one button to choose  the highest power level you can  the game relies on this system above all  else but then  once you've reached the end game content  no pun intended  your understanding of your inventory is  vital  visiting the frozen lands with an item  to stop you freezing your butt off  becomes integral  on the flip side having a weapon attack  that deals gamma damage  can make an impossible mission  accomplishable  the nuance of the loot system has a  great deal of potential  on top of this by unlocking skill points  in the game we can now change our super  abilities to function slightly different  they're only tweaks  but we can build a character unique to  us then the mastery of min  maxing comes in in which you build an  adventure designed for one single job in  a full team  be honest did that bore you to tears or  did that make you want to grind for loot  for me it's the latter i want to build a  thor that can one tap an enemy with a  hammer throw  without a doubt this is the appeal of  marvel's avengers power leveling a hero  and putting together six builds for  every fight you can imagine  reaching perfection is the goal here  i use destiny as the best parallel as to  the direction of marvel's avengers  both share huge similarities the world  has hubs to visit at present that's the  anthill and the chimera  in here we can see the faction system at  work as we pick up missions  and gear in a never-ending cycle of  incremental improvement  the mundane grind continues through  daily and weekly challenges  over my 20 hours online i played a  mixture of alone with people from my  discord  and other complete randoms too and once  again this is where the game felt great  the social aspect of games like this  can't be understated  a weekly meet up with friends as you  switch your brains off and finish  missions together  i played with one random guy for three  hours before they sent me a dm  and we'll likely play together again  soon there's something about games like  this like marvel's avengers that bring  people together  and as a guy who plays fortnite this  interaction  was humbling another aspect which may be  new to you  is um waiting yeah it's not great  on numerous occasions you will be  waiting in an elevator or sat  on the quinjet waiting for a mission to  begin it can feel like forever but once  again those people who play these types  of games  know that this is part of the cycle  things need to load and on console at  least  it takes a great deal of time i timed  one mission which had over three minutes  of load times either waiting in the  quinjet or hidden away in an elevator  next gen could help this issue i believe  but on the ps4 at least right now  waiting is not great here's the biggest  thing to take about the marvel's  avengers game  it isn't finished it will likely never  be finished and i know that sounds  strange  this is a game as a service which will  continually be  patched and iterated upon only this week  we found out that the new heroes are  coming which are clint and katie and  their hawkeye alter egos  those will be free updates which add a  backstory  hopefully to the quality of the campaign  and then they become whole new  superheroes we have to learn how to  fight with  and learn the skills of the thought of  shooting arrows in game right now  seems great and remember even more  characters are continually coming to the  game  whether that's black panther or if  you're on playstation we're gonna get  spider-man  by adding new characters the game  becomes increasingly replayable  and if we have a new superhero to flex  with then maybe we'll go out of our way  and use real money to buy a skin  too how do you feel about that so much  more is promised for the game and if  they get things right  marvel's avengers can be something very  very special  so to summarize the sublime story  content and top-notch voice acting the  set-piece boss fights in the campaign  bring marvel's characters to life  and the addictive loot system all makes  this game  a great experience right now but there  are weaknesses too with a focus on  monetizing customers who've already paid  full price for the game  through skins and emotes a lack of  challenge beyond button bashing online  and a monotony many people won't stick  around to play through  marvel's avengers is far from a final  version but the foundations in place  are strong my advice right now is to not  buy the game just yet  pick it up when more content is  available unless  you're into the loot grind like me and  if you are  i'll see you on the battlefield i'm adam  from playstation grenade  it's been a pleasure hopefully this has  helped in some way shape or form  i'll see you next time  you

